                                                "sense_id": "dbae373c-776f-353d-b4d2-6ace42e7f961",
                                                "text": "They addict themselves to the civil law."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "01b9e2cd-e9eb-4855-8413-c551498d0ca8",
                                                "sense_id": "dbae373c-776f-353d-b4d2-6ace42e7f961",
                                                "text": "Having resided some time in this place, we returned to the other country-house which we had left, where lord B— addicted himself so much to hunting, and other male diversions, that I began to think he neglected me […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f90b1804-ecd3-350f-b061-d815b25e2f80",
                                        "entry_id": "3c4addc1-21ad-34da-8453-04bd2cc6edb7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To bind (a person or thing) to the service of something."
                                        ],
